\pard\plain \fi720\sl288\slmult1\ltrch\loch {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 He\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92d been wounded in unexpected ways. He\u8217\'92d failed himself many times. He saw in every stranger\u8217\'92s face a look of pained reproach, sad and weary, because everyone had been through worse shit than he had, or was going through it presently, or was about to step in it real bad. Unless they were rich. Rich peoples faces were soft, unless the marriage was bad. Anyways, he didn\u8217\'92t like painting rich folks. It was a great pity that they were the only ones who could pay. In what kind of world should a young man make a living painting rich people\u8217\'92s faces while the poor disappear to history? It wasn\u8217\'92t right. Wasn\u8217\'92t right at all.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 He was deeply jealous.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 He pitied himself. He pitied other people too, in the way that old people pity other people\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 a sort of: I\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92m sorry you have to see me like this; if you\u8217\'92d known me back then I was much more handsome and vibrant and we would have been fast friends, but I understand that you want nothing to do with me, and honestly I don\u8217\'92t want anything to do with you because Life hasn\u8217\'92t yet stabbed you in the gut and so you don\u8217\'92t really know who you are yet.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 He knew who he was. He was a painter, and didn\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t want to be.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 He was young, but he knew that a person is capable of doing incredible things to another person. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1  Every person past a certain age is a walking pit of guilt and shame, or else scarred from people who are. The woman sitting the chair in the corner was well, well past that certain age.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1  The room was dark. Her corner was dark. Her blurry eyes reflected the shine of sunbeams streaming in from the single window. She watched dust motes swirl through the . His entrance had stirred them up. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You must be the new painter,\u8221\'94 she said to him. \u8220\'93Your name?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Mandri,\u8221\'94 he replied.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Mandriiii,\u8221\'94 she mumbled, her voice trailing into a crackling gurgle. \u8220\'93Come in, come in, come in. The young Vigram craves your indulgence in the dining room.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93And who are you?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I am Pel.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Vigram\u8217\'92s mother?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I am not certain of our relation.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 She held out her crinkly hand and \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93The dining room.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 The blackwood interior was lit with country charm, lived-inness, hearth, twisted fire-irons in the shapes , sitting in }
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93The young Vigram crave\u8217\'92s your indulgence in the dining room.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 She gestured towards the doorway beside her. }}